  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(t)=5t$ represent the rate at which water enters the tank, and let $V(T)$ be the total volume of water in the tank after $T$ minutes.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nV(T)=V(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(T) & =V(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =40+{\\int }_{0}^{T}5t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={40+(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =40+\\frac{5{T}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable  $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nV(t)=40+\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2}.\n$$",
